<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laredo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laredo is a city on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, facing Nuevo Laredo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. It was founded in 1755 by Tomás Sánchez as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-escandon">José de Escandón</a>'s colonisation of Nuevo Santander, and in 1840 it was the claimed seat of the short-lived Republic of the Rio Grande. Today it is one of the busiest land ports on the border between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and Mexico.</p></div>
